---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import { GITHUB_URL, LINKEDIN_URL } from '../consts';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Daniel Tripp is a software engineer working on distributed systems and database infrastructure."
	pubDate={new Date('November 09 2026')}
	hideDate
>
	<p>
		I'm Daniel, and I build the systems other systems depend on. Distributed systems, databases,
		infrastructure that has to be right at three in the morning. And I put AI to work on all of
		it, every day.
	</p>

	<p>
		At Reddit, I built the machinery behind nearly 200 production PostgreSQL clusters: a Kubernetes
		operator that turned a ticket queue into self-service, so teams got the database they needed
		without waiting on anyone. I built the controller that keeps 100+ services inside Aurora's
		5,000-connection limit, led their migration from PgBouncer to PgCat, and held the pager for
		PostgreSQL, Redis, Cassandra and Zookeeper. At Google, I built observability for data
		pipelines at a scale most people only read about.
	</p>

	<p>
		I've contributed to etcd, and I love the hard questions underneath it all: how consensus,
		replication and failure handling hold up when real traffic shows up. That's the work I do
		best, and the work I'd choose.
	</p>

	<p>
		AI is where I'm pushing hardest. I run coding agents all day, connect them to real tools over
		MCP, and trace every step so I know exactly what they cost and what they get right. I'm
		building toward engineering where I set the direction and agents do the heavy lifting, and
		I'm getting there fast.
	</p>

	<p>
		When I'm not at the keyboard I'm bouldering, playing piano, playing chess, or somewhere new,
		often on a cruise ship. Same approach everywhere: find the hard problem, enjoy it, solve it.
		You can find me on <a href={LINKEDIN_URL}>LinkedIn</a> and <a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a>,
		or follow along by RSS.
	</p>
</Layout>
